Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Controls and interpretation", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5194ff48-8c9c-40ff-a190-3c1a0b843f6e"],

Cell["\<\
Iteration k shows A^k e1, A^k e2, A^k e3; k = 0 shows the original standard \
basis. The three colored checkboxes hide or show each vector and its \
components independently. Show Q adds the unit columns of the QR factor \
without changing A^k.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d95b6d88-04bf-4d3e-81bf-a66c33ab09f0"],

Cell["\<\
The logarithmic Zoom in / out slider works after rotation as well. It spans \
many orders of magnitude. Fit vectors restores the default scale for the \
current iteration; Unit scale brings the eigenvectors and the Q columns into \
view. Drag the plot to rotate it about the origin. The camera is retained \
when controls change.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b07106dd-0612-4dbc-be99-177c0cf56f9c"],

Cell["\<\
Pale arrows decompose a vector along the eigenvector directions. At k = 0 \
their coefficients are the columns of S^-1; at iteration k the j-th \
coefficient is multiplied by lambda_j^k. For orthogonal eigenvectors these \
are perpendicular projections. For nonorthogonal eigenvectors they are the \
components of an oblique decomposition, so dot products alone would be \
incorrect.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"802211d1-1fc4-45be-ad03-d30fa26cb434"],

Cell["\<\
Grey direction guides are visual references and have no length scale. Unit \
eigenvector arrows and all A^k e_i and Q arrows have their true lengths. If a \
vector leaves the zoomed window, a labeled clipped line replaces its \
arrowhead. Axes and matrix entries retain physical units.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d5993ba2-8206-450a-a782-5d484f354963"],

Cell["\<\
QR is computed at extra working precision, with nonnegative diagonal entries \
in R. If A^k is singular, an orthonormal completion in Q is not unique. \
Complex eigenvectors and Jordan blocks are outside the input model of this \
real, diagonalizable 3D visualization.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9f638bd1-df56-4d26-80f2-757456ce69c6"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
},
